      "note": [
        "From 2014 reported occupational data for the revised standard for Swedish Occupational Classification 2012 ( SSYK 2012). SSYK 2012 replaces the previous version , SSYK96 . This means that comparison between 2014 and previous years should not be done.\r\n",
        "For employees aged 16-64 in 2014 relates most occupations , 74 percent , conditions in the reference year or the year after . 19 percent of the data is imputed using a model based on the occupational code (according SSYK 96 ) the individual had in the register previously . This means that there may be jobs in industries or sectors where they appear abnormal . The previous code used can be up to five years old.",
        "For employees in municipalities and county councils The occupational variable SSYK is connected from an AID Label-code. 2018, updates have been made in the AID code, which has led to certain changes among SSYK groups. Therefore, comparisons using SSYK before and after 2018 must be done with caution when looking at municipalities and county councils and also the public sector and entire labour market, especially occupations that are common in municipalities and county councils."
      ],
